  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>Kx</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mfrac><mi>dv</mi><mi>dx</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>integrating both sides<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8211;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, using work-energy theorem&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>KE</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8733;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p>"
